abstract: "daf-jev is a modular, composable Python client and decision toolkit for the TypeSafe Jev (System One) API, which turns generated text into typed machine decisions. One HTTP endpoint exposes three question primitives — noul (a 0-1 probability), choice (an option drawn from a probability distribution), and score (a rating on ordered rubric levels). On top of the typed answers the package provides pure-logic composition patterns (composite_score, confidence_gate, route, pick), a concurrent batch Evaluator, confidence-calibration statistics, a CLI, a Model Context Protocol (MCP) server, an agent skill, runnable examples, a live-API benchmark suite, a figure registry, and a reproducible {{TOKEN}}-parameterized manuscript pipeline. Archived on Zenodo as software."
